  "_doc": "Figma variable <-> code token. Code is canonical for VALUES; this map records only the correspondence. Filled by hand from a live read, by whoever is doing the work — there is no skill that sweeps the file, because a scheduled sweep would imply an authority the design canvas does not have. See ../README.md. A variable with `code: null` is drift — Figma has a variable with no token behind it. JOIN KEY: `variableId` is file-local and ephemeral, and it is what this map uses today because the source file is NOT published as a library. Every variable does already carry a `variableKey`; those are deliberately withheld until the file is published, so nobody mistakes them for a working library join. Re-read the ids after any operation that recreates variables. Also note NOTHING GATES THIS MAP — see ADR 0002.",
